From d94732cfa3098e738c33790c50b2a67b5e153f82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Denys Fedoryshchenko <denys.f@collabora.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 16:01:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] CHROMIUM: dri: cast strrchr result to char * in megadriver_stub.c

With glibc-2.43 / C23, string functions (such as strrchr) return const-qualified
pointers if the input argument is a pointer to a const-qualified type.
Because info.dli_fname is const char *, strrchr returns const char *, which
discards qualifiers when assigned to driver_name (char *). Cast the result to
char * to fix the compilation error.

This is a downstream-only compatibility fix for the legacy megadriver_stub.c
file (which is no longer present in modern upstream Mesa).

Reference:
https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/info-gnu/2026-01/msg00005.html

Change-Id: I673953d49d9fbfdc56a3bc3ef7c4b64c3266b123
---
 src/mesa/drivers/dri/common/megadriver_stub.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mesa/drivers/dri/common/megadriver_stub.c b/src/mesa/drivers/dri/common/megadriver_stub.c
index d085080a197..4e4aeb43ef9 100644
--- a/src/mesa/drivers/dri/common/megadriver_stub.c
+++ b/src/mesa/drivers/dri/common/megadriver_stub.c
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ megadriver_stub_init(void)
       return;
 
    /* Search for the last '/' character in the path. */
-   driver_name = strrchr(info.dli_fname, '/');
+   driver_name = (char *) strrchr(info.dli_fname, '/');
    if (driver_name != NULL) {
       /* Skip '/' character */
       driver_name++;
-- 
